py. So the design accepts this behavior. Extra baseline error in D-4 is a consequence of the acceptance fixture copying only `test, contracts`. The design's D-4 probably still passes since it checks substring presence.\n\nHmm, but should the baseline failure for a3-runner be suppressed when the import cannot resolve? The design says run and require pass. If the temp copy lacks scripts, it fails. The design/acceptance pair is consistent enough: acceptance D-4 only requires the specific line. But a strict reviewer running `node scripts/check-defects.mjs --root $t --strict` on a copy without scripts would see 2 errors. Since acceptance explicitly lists expected lines and says \"stdout 含 ...\", it's fine.\n\nHowever, there might be a cleaner approach: rewrite relative imports to point into `root` (the real repo path) rather than the copied repro dir — i.e., resolve spec against `path.join(root, relative dir of reproFile)`? That's the same thing (reproFile is under root). So no improvement.\n\nAlternatively, use the real repo when importing the *script*? No; can't distinguish.\n\nI'll leave as is — it matches the design and acceptance.\n\nNow D-5 and D-6 verification.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b6ed676071dd96d1dddec21a8d4b","_messageId":"01a1b6ef53757980967a616d7f1e521e","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b6ed676071dd96d1dddec21a8d4b","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b6ef53757980967a616d7f1e521e","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b6ef53757980967a616d7f1e521e","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b6ef-5375-7980-967a-616f939c46a9","traceparent":"00-d8eabdeed6a792af6860e0cc046eb175-76376bad59b4e1b9-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b6ed-6347-7996