 for each check, fenced code block with commands, then \"期望：...\" prose (not bullets). Hmm but the note says \"Keep one check per '## ' section\". That contradicts 001 having `###` per check.\n\nMaybe the parser used is different: perhaps it parses `##` OR `###` as check headers. exit 2, zero commands extracted — why zero? Possibly because the parser requires the fence directly after `## ` heading and current file's `## A. 总入口` are group headings, so each `##` section has no fence at its start... but if it also parses `###`, it'd find them. Unless it only splits on `## ` (level 2 exactly). Then task 001 would also yield zero commands (since `## 0.` sections contain `###`), unless the parser treats `##` sections and finds fences anywhere in the section.\n\nHmm, if parser takes each level-2 section and finds first fenced block, then 001's `## 0. 辅助函数` has a fence → 1 command. `## 1. 通用要求` has no fence until `### V-01` which is inside section 1 → its first fence. That would give ~9 commands for 001, not 60. That's weird for a \"one check per ## section\" instruction.\n\nMaybe the parser works on `###`? Then 001 gives ~60 checks, 002 gives 5+... Actually 002 has `### A-1`, etc. That should work too.\n\nLet me find the CI runner script. Maybe it's in .collab/studio or somewhere. Let me search for ci-results.json or \"commands extracted\".","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b6f5857e79d381455250fb276344","_messageId":"01a1b6f5cf9972dd9e6248c126b9a2d8","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b6f5857e79d381455250fb276344","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b6f5cf9972dd9e6248c126b9a2d8","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b6f5cf9972dd9e6248c126b9a2d8","codebuddy.a