{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b6f9-ed13-7709-9639-ddb23509ec2b","session_id":"01a1b6f5-80e5-79d6-a660-1b272ac4a004","message":{"id":"01a1b6f9ed1377099639ddb0b543ff3a","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the scope was extended in the task-graph (blueprint) for two one-line fixes: check-ci CRLF tolerance and a traceability test fixture AC-005→AC-006 (because AC-005 is now covered by T-002, so the test asserting AC-005 planned would break).\n\nBut the acceptance.md E-2 regex was not updated to allow these two paths. That's why E-2 fails. Since I'm rewriting acceptance.md (authorized by the note), I should include these two paths in the allowed set — matching the extended write_scope in task-graph. This is consistent with design (task-graph is authoritative per brief). Indeed, design.md's write_scope is stale but task-graph was updated by the orchestrator/human.\n\nCareful: \"不要自行发明任何字段、版本号或章节名\" — fine.\n\nNow, also `.gitattributes` is allowed by the task graph but not created (good, we don't need it).\n\nNow let me also double check that the E-2 `git status --porcelain` part passes: currently there are modified .collab/tasks/002 files (allowed) and live.json (allowed under .collab/tasks/002/). Let me check.\n\nAlso check the last commit 3965eb9 modified .collab/tasks/002/* and two source files — consistent.\n\nWait, actually 3965eb9's message says \"fix(dev): repair after CI failure\" and includes impl.md, logs, run.json, state.json, notice.json, input-ledger, inputs — those are under .collab/tasks/002/, fine.\n\nNow let me run the full test (A-5) and then rewrite acceptance.md.\n\nActually, before rewriting: the current acceptance.md (264 lines) — I need to restructure while preserving content and updating E-2. Let me read the whole current acceptance.md again carefully (I have it above). I'll write a new version.\n\nDesign for the new file:\n\n```\n# T-002 验收标准\n\n（intro prose: 对应 AC-005、执行环境、通用约定）\n\n## 0. 通用约定与期望格式\n### X-00 ...? \n```\n\nHmm. Let me la